{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BarParityZeta4Swap"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_barEven_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_barEven_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L235-L239","doc":"Same, for the B-shape: a value of `barEven` pins `z² − z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_barEven_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_barEven_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L225-L233","doc":"The **contrast with 4₁**, stated as the obstruction it is: for the\nfigure-eight `barEven ω = 1` is *rational*, whereas a 5₂ A-shape with rational\n`barEven` would force its cubic to have the corresponding rational root. This\nlemma is the reusable half — `barEven` determines `z² − z` on the A-shape, so a\nrational `barEven` pins a quadratic relation that the cubic must also satisfy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52_cubics_agree_in_char_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52_cubics_agree_in_char_two","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L215-L223","doc":"**The hypothesis is necessary, and Lean is what caught that.** In\ncharacteristic 2 the two cubics COINCIDE — `−2z² = 0` and `3z = z` — so both\nread `z³ + z + 1 = 0` and a single element satisfies both. The distinctness of\nthe 5₂ shape classes is a characteristic-0 fact about this knot, not a formal\nconsequence of the two polynomials being different as symbols. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_not_shape52B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_not_shape52B","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L198-L213","doc":"**The two 5₂ shapes are distinct** away from characteristic 2: subtracting\nthe cubics forces `2z = 0`, and with `2 ≠ 0` that gives `z = 0`, which\n`shape52A_ne_zero` excludes. This is the algebraic form of the measured\n`z₁ = z₃ ≠ z₂`. The `2 ≠ 0` hypothesis is NOT decoration — see the next\ntheorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52_reconstruct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52_reconstruct","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L194-L196","doc":"Both coordinates together recover `2z`, as for any shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L187-L190","doc":"**B-shape, bar-odd:** `barOdd z = −z² + 3z − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_barEven_eq_cyclotomic_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_barEven_eq_cyclotomic_six","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L180-L185","doc":"**The B-shape's bar-even coordinate IS `Φ₆`** — the polynomial whose\nvanishing defines the 4₁ cusp shape. An identity, not an interpretation: it is\nimmediate from `shape52B_inv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L175-L178","doc":"**B-shape, bar-even:** `barEven z = z² − z + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L170-L173","doc":"**A-shape, bar-odd:** `barOdd z = −z² + 3z − 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L165-L168","doc":"**A-shape, bar-even:** `barEven z = z² − z + 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_inv","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L158-L161","doc":"The B-shape's inverse is the polynomial `(z − 1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_mul_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_mul_inv","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L153-L156","doc":"`z · (z − 1)² = 1` on the B-shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_inv","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L148-L151","doc":"The A-shape's inverse is the polynomial `z² − 2z + 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_mul_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_mul_inv","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L142-L146","doc":"`z · (z² − 2z + 3) = 1` on the A-shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52B_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L137-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.shape52A_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L132-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.cyclotomic_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.cyclotomic_six","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L126-L128","doc":"`Φ₆`, the sixth cyclotomic polynomial, named so the `barEven` coincidence\nbelow can be stated in its own terms rather than as a bare quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.IsShape52B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.IsShape52B","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L122-L124","doc":"The **B-shape** of 5₂ — carried by the remaining tetrahedron (`z₂`): a root\nof `z³ − 2z² + z − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.IsShape52A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.IsShape52A","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCuspShapeBarParity.lean#L118-L120","doc":"The **A-shape** of 5₂ — carried by two of the three ideal tetrahedra\n(`z₁ = z₃`): a root of `z³ − 2z² + 3z − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}